``peat pillage`` can now unlock encrypted volumes on disk images: BitLocker on Windows (with ``Unlock-BitLocker``) and Linux, and LUKS on Linux (with ``cryptsetup``), read-only. Passwords and BitLocker recovery passwords are read from a file with the new ``--password-file`` option, or prompted for in a terminal, and are never logged or passed on the command line. On Linux, pillage now searches every partition on an image instead of only the first one, images without a partition table, and LVM volumes (including LVM inside LUKS, like a default encrypted Ubuntu install), and mounts them in a ``pillage_temp_<random>`` directory.
